-// ../cursor-plugins/dist/git-sparse-clone.js
-/**
- * Sparse + partial clone support for plugin repositories.
- *
- * Plugins that live in a subdirectory of a large monorepo previously required
- * fetching every blob in the repo at depth 1, which routinely exceeded the
- * 30s plugin clone timeout. These helpers implement the
- * "partial clone + cone-mode sparse checkout" strategy:
- *
- * ```
- * git init
- * git sparse-checkout set --cone -- <dirs>
- * git fetch --depth 1 --filter=blob:none <url> <sha>
- * git checkout FETCH_HEAD
- * ```
- *
- * `--filter=blob:none` makes the server omit file contents;
- the checkout then
- * lazily fetches only the blobs needed for the sparse worktree. Servers that
- * do not support filtering (no `uploadpack.allowFilter`) ignore the filter
- * with a warning and send a full pack, so behavior degrades gracefully to a
- * plain shallow clone. Additional directories can be materialized later with
- * `git sparse-checkout add` (or the whole tree with `git sparse-checkout
- * disable`), which lazily fetches missing blobs from the promisor remote that
- * git records for the fetch URL.
- *
- * Known limitation: files reachable only via symlinks that point outside the
- * materialized directories are absent from a sparse worktree. Plugins relying
- * on such symlinks already fail at install time today (the installed copy
- * escapes the plugin dir), so only repo-local preview of those plugins is
- * affected;
- they are skipped with a warning like any other unreadable plugin.
- *
- * @packageDocumentation
- */
